{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q415831","formula":"Cu₂(AsO₄)(OH)","hill":"AsCu2HO5","elements":["H","O","Cu","As"],"composition":{"H":1.0,"O":5.0,"As":1.0,"Cu":2.0},"names":{"en":"Olivenite","ru":"Оливенит","uk":"Олівеніт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Olivenite is a copper arsenate mineral, formula Cu2AsO4OH. It crystallizes in the monoclinic system (pseudo-orthorhombic), and is sometimes found in small brilliant crystals of simple prismatic habit terminated by domal faces. More commonly, it occurs as globular aggregates of acicular crystals, these fibrous forms often having a velvety luster; sometimes it is lamellar in structure, or soft and earthy. A characteristic feature, and one to which the name alludes (German, Olivenerz, of A. G. Werner, 1789), is the olive-green color, which varies in shade from blackish-green in the crystals to almost white in the finely fibrous variety known as woodcopper.","ru":"Оливенит — вторичный минерал из класса арсенатов. Название получил за свою окраску. Относится к группе оливенита, которая состоит из шести минералов: Оливенит (Cu2(AsO4)(OH)) Адамин (Zn2(AsO4)(OH)) Либетенит (Cu2(PO4)(OH)) Цинколибетенит (CuZn(PO4)(OH)) Эвеит (Mn2(AsO4)(OH)) Эвхроит (Cu2(AsO4)(OH)·3H2O) Все минералы данной группы кристаллизуются в моноклинной сингонии.","uk":"Олівеніт — мінерал, гідроарсенат міді острівної будови."},"fame":24,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q415831","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olivenite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9E%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4